---
description: Security rules for secure-by-default development and operations
globs: ["security/**", "**/*.tf", "**/*.yml", "**/*.yaml", "**/*.py", "**/*.ts", "**/*.js", "**/*.go", "**/*.rb"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Design for least privilege: scope tokens/roles narrowly and avoid broad wildcards.
- Threat model user-facing changes; ensure authZ and authN are explicit and centrally enforced.
- Validate and sanitize all untrusted input; encode output at sinks to prevent injection.
- Enforce HTTPS/TLS everywhere; disable weak ciphers/protocols where configurable.
- Log security events with correlation IDs but never secrets/PII; set retention appropriately.
- Fail closed on security controls; prefer explicit denial over permissive defaults.
- Keep dependencies updated; gate merges with vulnerability checks and pin where needed.
- Provide safe defaults for crypto (modern algorithms, strong randomness, rotation paths).
